<title>USA: Penn National Q1 net flat after charge.</title>
<headline>Penn National Q1 net flat after charge.</headline>
<dateline>WYOMISSING, Pa. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     1997     1996</p>
<p>Total revenues				 $22,820  $14,560</p>
<p>Total operating expenses		    19,144   12,521</p>
<p>Income from operations			 3,676    2,039</p>
<p>Total other income (expenses)		(814)	 54</p>
<p>Income (loss) before income taxes	  2,862    2,093</p>
<p>Taxes on income (benefit)		    1,178	854</p>
<p>Net Income before extraordinary item    $1,684   $1,239</p>
<p>Extraordinary item - Loss on early</p>
<p>extinguishment of debt, net of taxes</p>
<p>  of $260					    383	 -</p>
<p>Net Income					$1,301   $1,239</p>
<p>Net Income per share before</p>
<p> extraordinary item			    $0.11    $0.09</p>
<p>Net income per share			   $0.09    $0.09</p>
<p>Weighted average number of common</p>
<p> shares outstanding(a)			14,912   13,302</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Penn National Gaming Inc.</p>
<p>(a) The weighted average number of shares outstanding have been adjusted to reflect the May 1996 3-for-2 stock split, the December 1996 2-for-1 stock split, and the company's February 1997 offering of 1,725,000 shares of common.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610 ))</p>
